\title{MVCens: Matrix-Variate Models with Censoring and Asymmetry}
\description{
MVCens provides a common interface for generating, fitting, and evaluating
matrix-variate normal, censored, skewed, and heavy-tailed models. The main
user workflow is built around \code{\link[=mv_random]{mv_random()}}, \code{\link[=mv_fit]{mv_fit()}}, and
\code{\link[=mv_monte_carlo]{mv_monte_carlo()}}. Lower-level density, log-likelihood, moment, and
reference-parameter functions are also available for direct calculations.
}
\section{Main workflow}{

\itemize{
\item Use \code{\link[=mv_random]{mv_random()}} to generate matrix-valued observations.
\item Use \code{\link[=mv_fit]{mv_fit()}} to estimate a registered model by ECM.
\item Use \code{\link[=mv_monte_carlo]{mv_monte_carlo()}} to assess an estimator in repeated samples.
}
}

\section{Supported models}{

The high-level API recognizes \code{MVN}, \code{MVNC}, \code{MVSN}, \code{MVSNC}, \code{MVST},
\code{MVRSN}, and \code{MVREN}. Generation is additionally available for \code{MVNIG} and
\code{MVVG}. Censored models use \code{cc} as the censoring indicator and \code{LS} as the
array of censoring limits.
}

\section{Numerical convention}{

Matrix observations are stored in arrays of dimensions \code{p} by \code{q} by \code{n}.
Covariance structures use a \code{p} by \code{p} row component (\code{Sigma}) and a \code{q} by
\code{q} column component (\code{Psi}). Consult each function's help page for its
model-specific arguments and return value.
}

